Cudy TR3600 v1: use the vendor Wi-Fi MAC address layout

The board DTS derived the radio addresses as base + 3 (2.4 GHz) and
base + 2 (5 GHz).  The vendor layout, verified on a production unit, is:

  LAN / gmac1 : base + 0
  WAN / gmac0 : base + 1
  2.4 GHz     : base + 0   (shares the LAN address)
  5 GHz       : base + 0x10

The base address is the only MAC stored in the bdinfo partition (at
0xde00, followed by 0xff), so the offsets must reproduce the vendor
assignment rather than be chosen merely to be unique.

Reported-by: Ylarod <https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/24596>

Signed-off-by: TR3600 build kit <noreply@example.com>
---
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987b-cudy-tr3600-v1.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987b-cudy-tr3600-v1.dts
@@ -143,16 +143,19 @@
 			nvmem-cells = <&eeprom_factory_0>;
 			nvmem-cell-names = "eeprom";
 
-			/* Offset 3 keeps the 2.4 GHz MAC distinct from LAN. */
+			/*
+			 * Vendor layout, verified on a production unit: the 2.4 GHz
+			 * radio shares the LAN/base address and 5 GHz is base + 0x10.
+			 */
 			band@0 {
 				reg = <0>;
-				nvmem-cells = <&macaddr_bdinfo_de00 3>;
+				nvmem-cells = <&macaddr_bdinfo_de00 0>;
 				nvmem-cell-names = "mac-address";
 			};
 
 			band@1 {
 				reg = <1>;
-				nvmem-cells = <&macaddr_bdinfo_de00 2>;
+				nvmem-cells = <&macaddr_bdinfo_de00 16>;
 				nvmem-cell-names = "mac-address";
 			};
 		};
